&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hey there! &lt;br&gt;We’re &lt;a href=&quot;https://feverup.com/&quot;&gt;Fever&lt;/a&gt;, the world’s leading tech platform for culture and live entertainment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission? To democratize access to culture and entertainment. With our proprietary cutting-edge technology and data-driven approach, we’re revolutionizing the way people engage with live entertainment. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every month, our platform inspires over 300 million people in +55 countries (and counting) to discover unforgettable experiences while also empowering event creators with our data and technology, helping them scale, innovate, and enhance their events to reach new audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our results? We’ve teamed up with major industry leaders like Netflix, F.C. Barcelona, and Primavera Sound, presented international award-winning experiences, and are backed by several leading global investors! Impressive, right?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To achieve our mission, we are looking for bar-raisers with a hands-on mindset who are eager to help shape the future of entertainment!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to be part of the experience?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, let’s discuss this role and what you will do to help achieve Fever’s mission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the &lt;strong&gt;Fever Originals team&lt;/strong&gt;, you will leverage data, market insights, and strong commercial instincts to create one-of-a-kind events and experiences that enable people to enjoy unforgettable moments. Our goal is to develop and scale innovative experiences while building strong relationships with venues, partners, and industry stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you&#39;ll work with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You will join our office in Berlin, working closely with internal teams while directly engaging with partners, providers, and venues across the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will play a key part in growing Fever’s pipeline of &lt;strong&gt;original events&lt;/strong&gt;. A significant part of your work will involve identifying, developing, and negotiating partnerships with venues and external stakeholders, while collaborating cross-functionally with departments such as Marketing, Operations, and Finance to bring experiences to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team you will join is young, ambitious, and highly collaborative, composed of top profiles from companies such as McKinsey, Amazon, Google, KKR, Cirque du Soleil, PSG, and Roland Garros. Team members bring diverse cultural backgrounds and share a strong entrepreneurial mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Junior Project Manager, you will work closely with your team to develop, launch, and manage Fever Originals experiences from concept to execution. The role combines project management, commercial development, and strategic partnerships, with a strong emphasis on venue negotiations, relationship management, and networking within the local entertainment and events ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you join Fever, you will receive training and coaching to help you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop new business opportunities, including sourcing venues, partners, and collaborators for new event concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead venue sourcing and contract negotiations, securing optimal terms and building long-term partnerships with strategic venues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the financial and operational feasibility of our events by analyzing and reporting on key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue growth by optimizing ticket sales strategies and identifying opportunities to expand event reach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze business performance, including P&amp;amp;L tracking, forecasting, and operational efficiency improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Marketing, Operations, Legal, and Finance teams to ensure successful event launches and smooth operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale successful experiences across additional cities and markets by building replicable operational models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high-quality experiences, maintaining strong standards for customer satisfaction and operational delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines a&lt;strong&gt; strong commercial mindset, relationship-building abilities, and analytical thinking, with a proactive approach to developing partnerships and growing the business.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in project management, operations, consulting, business development, partnerships, or similar roles (this role is not primarily suited for traditional event planners)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;German &lt;/strong&gt;on a native level as well as fluency in &lt;strong&gt;English &lt;/strong&gt;with excellent communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation and networking skills, with the ability to build meaningful partnerships: you’re not afraid of picking up the phone and pitching to potential new partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational and project management skills, with the ability to plan, prioritize, and drive multiple workstreams to successful completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and results-driven, able to perform under pressure, take ownership, and manage several high-impact projects in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain strong relationships with venues, partners, brands, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills, with the ability to use data to guide decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly solution-oriented, able to identify challenges and develop practical strategies to resolve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work and thrive in fast-paced environments and willingness to grow within the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to have a real impact in a high-growth global category leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;40% discount on all Fever events and experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meal tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in the heart of the city, with possible travel across our markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsibility from day one and professional and personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great work environment with a young, international team of talented people to work with!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Hiring Process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 30 min video call with one of our Talent Acquisition Managers, to better understand your career plan, assess cultural fit and answer any questions you may have&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 60 min online test with three topics: logic, analytics and written understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 30 min video call with your future manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 45 min in-person conversation with your future manager, including questions about your profile and a business case presentation (to be prepared in advance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a team of highly effective, motivated, and entrepreneurial professionals who move fast, take ownership, and get things done. Cultural fit means being humble, open to feedback, and willing to learn, while approaching challenges as opportunities and making decisions based on data and insight. We value individuals who are hands-on, collaborative, and able to prioritize what truly drives results. We encourage applicants from diverse and unconventional backgrounds, especially those who bring curiosity, a willingness to learn, and the drive to make a meaningful impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in &lt;strong&gt;Berlin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Fulltime #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thank you for considering joining Fever. We cannot wait to learn more about you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to learn more about us: &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://newsroom.feverup.com/en-US/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://newsroom.feverup.com/en-UKI/208389-goldman-sachs-asset-management-leads-227m-investment-in-live-entertainment-tech-startup-fever&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Fever&#39;s Blog&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://tech.eu/2023/02/02/fever-raises-110-million-in-new-round-at-1-8-billion-valuation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Tech.Eu&lt;/a&gt; |&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2019/08/04/data-driven-events-discovery-and-planning-startup-fever-raises-35-million-led-by-rakuten/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2019/08/04/data-driven-events-discovery-and-planning-startup-fever-raises-35-million-led-by-rakuten/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;TechCrunch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fever is committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workspace where everyone&#39;s background and ideas count. Our main goal is to find the best possible talent regardless of place of birth, racial or ethnic origin, gender, gender identity, religion, opinion, sexual orientation, disability, pregnancy, marital status, age or caring responsibilities. We encourage everyone to apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require any kind of accommodation during the selection process please contact our Talent team so we can help you by providing a welcoming and seamless journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to know more about how Fever processes your personal data, click here&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cIzPP7QJGht5LAGKkRGQP8fxh-Z4Mfph2JhGSvhd8zM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.y7rpsj7nzave&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Fever - Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

